        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0527" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg431"/>

                <head>No. 321.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-07"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 7, 1872</date>.
                        (Received June 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 582.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The only military events I have to record
                    since my last general dispatch are the capture of Monterey, on the 31st ultimo,
                    and the defeat of the rebel generals Guerra and Marquez, near the city of
                    Durango, about the same date. Both events are as yet known only by brief
                    telegraphic dispatches, but it seems that the capture of Monterey was preceded
                    by a hard-fought battle, in which a portion of the army of General Corella was
                    routed, and that nothing is certainly known of the whereabouts of that
                    general.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
